OS), Neurovitae Center for Neuroscience, School of Medicine and Health Sciences, Institute of Translational Medicine (IMT), Universidad del Rosario, Bogot\u00e1 111221, Colombia."}]}}, {"fullName": "Androudi S", "lastName": "Androudi", "firstName": "Sofia", "initials": "S", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-5303-7793"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Ophthalmology, University Hospital of Larissa, 41334 Larissa, Greece."}]}}, {"fullName": "Kakoulidis P", "lastName": "Kakoulidis", "firstName": "Panos", "initials": "P", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-2980-2528"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Informatics and Telecommunications, School of Science, National and Kapodistrian University of Athens (NKUA), 15701 Athens, Greece."}]}}, {"fullName": "Tierradentro-Alape R", "lastName": "Tierradentro-Alape", "firstName": "Rafael", "initials": "R", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0009-0007-9410-3527"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Neuroscience Research Group (NEUROS), Neurovitae Center for Neuroscience, School of Medicine and Health Sciences, Institute of Translational Medicine (IMT), Universidad del Rosario, Bogot\u00e1 111221, Colombia."}]}}, {"fullName": "Kalogeropoulos D", "lastName": "Kalogeropoulos", "firstName": "Dimitrios", "initials": "D", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-6404-5409"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Ophthalmology, Stoke Mandeville Hospital, Buckinghamshire Healthcare NHS Foundation Trust, Mandeville Rd, Aylesbury HP21 8AL, UK."}]}}]}, "authorIdList": {"authorId": [{"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-6404-5409"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-8916-3276"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-5303-7793"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-0684-1989"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-2980-2528"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0009-0000-7798-3226"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0009-0007-9410-3527"}]}, "dataLinksTagsList": {"dataLinkstag": ["altmetrics", "supporting_data"]}, "journalInfo": {"issue": "10", "volume": "16", "journalIssueId": 4201796, "dateOfPublication": "2026 May", "monthOfPublication": 5, "yearOfPublication": 2026, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "Diagnostics (Basel)", "title": "Diagnostics (Basel, Switzerland)", "essn": "2075-4418", "issn": "2075-4418", "nlmid": "101658402", "isoabbreviation": "Diagnostics (Basel)"}, "printPublicationDate": "2026-05-01"}, "pubYear": "2026", "pageInfo": "1416", "abstractText": "The scope of the present study is to conduct a comprehensive review of the anatomy, function, major pathological conditions and clinical significance of ocular lymphatic vessels. In recent years, it has become evident that ocular lymphatics play a major role in the pathogenesis and progression of ocular disorders. Therefore, we delved into this emerging field and described newly proposed mechanisms that may explain the involvement of ocular lymphatics in healthy and pathological states. Lymphatics are present in a plethora of ocular tissues primarily under pathological conditions, including limbal stroma, optic nerve, ocular muscles, lacrimal glands and sclera. The conjunctiva contains an extensive lymphatic network, whereas the cornea and retina are typically devoid of lymphatic vessels under physiological conditions. Inflammatory conditions can give birth to nascent lymphatic vessel sprouting. Growing evidence emphasizes the role of ocular lymphatics in glaucoma pathogenesis, suggesting a previously unknown aqueous humor drainage pathway mediated by lymphatic contribution. This review is based mainly on evidence from animal and experimental models, as human clinical data remain limited; therefore, caution is warranted when translating these findings into clinical practice. By gaining insight into the mechanisms and the clinical significance of eye lymphatics, this review aims to address novel insights for future research and treatment of eye diseases, as well as to highlight a misconception that has persisted for decades in ophthalmology.", "affiliation": "School of Health Sciences, Faculty of Medicine, University of Ioannina, 45500 Ioannina, Greece.", "publicationStatus": "epublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Electronic", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["review-article", "Review", "Journal Article"]}, "keywordList": {"keyword": ["Lymphangiogenesis", "Aqueous Humor Drainage", "Ocular Lymphatics", "Ocular Fluid Homeostasis"]}, "fullTextUrlList": {"fullTextUrl": [{"availability": "Subscription required", "availabilityCode": "S", "documentStyle": "doi", "site": "DOI", "url": "https://doi.org/10.3390/diagnostics16101416"}, {"availability": "Open access", "availabilityCode": "OA", "documentStyle": "html", "site": "Europe_PMC", "url": "https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13205503"}, {"availability": "Open access", "availabilityCode": "OA", "documentStyle": "pdf", "site": "Europe_PMC", "url": "https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13205503?pdf=render"}]}, "isOpenAccess": "Y", "inEPMC": "Y", "inPMC": "Y", "citedByCount": 0, "hasReferences": "Y", "hasTextMinedTerms": "Y", "hasDbCrossReferences": "N", "hasPDF": "Y", "hasBook": "N", "hasSuppl": "N", "hasLabsLinks": "Y", "hasData": "Y", "license": "cc by", "authMan": "N", "epmcAuthMan": "N", "nihAuthMan": "N", "hasTMAccessionNumbers": "Y", "tmAccessionTypeList": {"accessionType": ["doi"]}, "dateOfCompletion": "2026-05-27", "dateOfCreation": "2026-05-27", "dateOfRevision": "2026-08-13", "electronicPublicationDate": "2026-05-07", "firstPublicationDate": "2026-05-07", "firstIndexDate": "2026-05-28", "fullTextReceivedDate": "2026-05-27", "hasEvaluations": "N"}, {"id": "34769057", "source": "MED", "pmid": "34769057", "pmcid": "PMC8583961", "fullTextIdList": {"fullTextId": ["PMC8583961"]}, "doi": "10.3390/ijms222111628", "title": "Corneal Lymphangiogenesis: Current Pathophysiological Understandings and Its Functional Role in Ocular Surface Disease.", "authorString": "Lee HK, Lee SM, Lee DI.", "authorList": {"author": [{"fullName": "Lee HK", "lastName": "Lee", "firstName": "Hyung-Keun", "initials": "HK", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-1123-2136"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Ophthalmology, Institute of Vision Research, Yonsei University College of Medicine, Seoul 06273, Korea."}]}}, {"fullName": "Lee SM", "lastName": "Lee", "firstName": "Sang-Mok", "initials": "SM", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-9018-8216"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Ophthalmology, HanGil Eye Hospital, Catholic Kwandong University College of Medicine, Incheon 21388, Korea."}]}}, {"fullName": "Lee DI", "lastName": "Lee", "firstName": "Dong-Ihll", "initials": "DI", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Medical School, Capital Medical University, Beijing 100069, China."}]}}]}, "authorIdList": {"authorId": [{"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-1123-2136"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-9018-8216"}]}, "dataLinksTagsList": {"dataLinkstag": ["altmetrics"]}, "journalInfo": {"issue": "21", "volume": "22", "journalIssueId": 3257590, "dateOfPublication": "2021 Oct", "monthOfPublication": 10, "yearOfPublication": 2021, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "Int J Mol Sci", "title": "International journal of molecular sciences", "essn": "1422-0067", "issn": "1422-0067", "nlmid": "101092791", "isoabbreviation": "Int J Mol Sci"}, "printPublicationDate": "2021-10-01"}, "pubYear": "2021", "pageInfo": "11628", "abstractText": "The cornea is a transparent and avascular tissue that plays a central role in light refraction and provides a physical barrier to the external environment. Corneal avascularity is a unique histological feature that distinguishes it from the other parts of the body. Functionally, corneal immune privilege critically relies on corneal avascularity. Corneal lymphangiogenesis is now recognized as a general pathological feature in many pathologies, including dry eye disease (DED), corneal allograft rejection, ocular allergy, bacterial and viral keratitis, and transient corneal edema. Currently, sizable data from clinical and basic research have accumulated on the pathogenesis and functional role of ocular lymphangiogenesis. However, because of the invisibility of lymphatic vessels, ocular lymphangiogenesis has not been studied as much as hemangiogenesis. We reviewed the basic mechanisms of lymphangiogenesis and summarized recent advances in the pathogenesis of ocular lymphangiogenesis, focusing on corneal allograft rejection and DED. In addition, we discuss future directions for lymphangiogenesis research.", "affiliation": "Department of Ophthalmology, Institute of Vision Research, Yonsei University College of Medicine, Seoul 06273, Korea.", "publicationStatus": "epublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Electronic", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["review-article", "Review", "Journal Article"]}, "meshHeadingList": {"meshHeading": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Cornea", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "abbreviation": "PA", "qualifierName": "pathology"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Lymphatic Vessels", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "PA", "qualifierName": "pathology"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Animals"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Humans"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Corneal Diseases", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "abbreviation": "PA", "qualifierName": "pathology"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Corneal Neovascularization", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "PA", "q