slin JW, Yang Y, Scallan JP, Sweat RS, Adderley SP, Murfee WL.", "authorList": {"author": [{"fullName": "Breslin JW", "lastName": "Breslin", "firstName": "Jerome W", "initials": "JW", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Molecular Pharmacology and Physiology, Morsani College of Medicine, University of South Florida, Tampa, Florida, USA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Yang Y", "lastName": "Yang", "firstName": "Ying", "initials": "Y", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Molecular Pharmacology and Physiology, Morsani College of Medicine, University of South Florida, Tampa, Florida, USA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Scallan JP", "lastName": "Scallan", "firstName": "Joshua P", "initials": "JP", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-1190-7308"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Molecular Pharmacology and Physiology, Morsani College of Medicine, University of South Florida, Tampa, Florida, USA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Sweat RS", "lastName": "Sweat", "firstName": "Richard S", "initials": "RS", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Biomedical Engineering, Tulane University, New Orleans, Tampa, Louisiana, USA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Adderley SP", "lastName": "Adderley", "firstName": "Shaquria P", "initials": "SP", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Molecular Pharmacology and Physiology, Morsani College of Medicine, University of South Florida, Tampa, Florida, USA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Murfee WL", "lastName": "Murfee", "firstName": "Walter L", "initials": "WL", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Biomedical Engineering, University of Florida, Gainesville, Florida, USA."}]}}]}, "authorIdList": {"authorId": [{"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-1190-7308"}]}, "dataLinksTagsList": {"dataLinkstag": ["altmetrics", "supporting_data"]}, "journalInfo": {"issue": "1", "volume": "9", "journalIssueId": 2761077, "dateOfPublication": "2018 Dec", "monthOfPublication": 12, "yearOfPublication": 2018, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "Compr Physiol", "title": "Comprehensive Physiology", "essn": "2040-4603", "issn": "2040-4603", "nlmid": "101574442", "isoabbreviation": "Compr Physiol"}, "printPublicationDate": "2018-12-01"}, "pubYear": "2018", "pageInfo": "207-299", "abstractText": "The lymphatic system is comprised of a network of vessels interrelated with lymphoid tissue, which has the holistic function to maintain the local physiologic environment for every cell in all tissues of the body. The lymphatic system maintains extracellular fluid homeostasis favorable for optimal tissue function, removing substances that arise due to metabolism or cell death, and optimizing immunity against bacteria, viruses, parasites, and other antigens. This article provides a comprehensive review of important findings over the past century along with recent advances in the understanding of the anatomy and physiology of lymphatic vessels, including tissue/organ specificity, development, mechanisms of lymph formation and transport, lymphangiogenesis, and the roles of lymphatics in disease. \u00a9 2019 American Physiological Society. Compr Physiol 9:207-299, 2019.", "affiliation": "Department of Molecular Pharmacology and Physiology, Morsani College of Medicine, University of South Florida, Tampa, Florida, USA.", "publicationStatus": "epublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Electronic", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["research-article", "Review", "Journal Article", "Research Support, N.I.H., Extramural"]}, "grantsList": {"grant": [{"agency": "NIA NIH HHS", "acronym": "AG", "grantId": "R01 AG049821", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIGMS NIH HHS", "acronym": "GM", "grantId": "R01 GM120774", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NHLBI NIH HHS", "acronym": "HL", "grantId": "R01 HL098215", "orderIn": 0}, {"agenc